{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 39, :comments ["In all of them the names of their places are mentioned, except for Ba'al Hanan son of Akhbor, because he had no known place — he had many enemies and would hide here today and there tomorrow, and did not dwell in any known place." "<b>And the name of his wife</b> — the name of his wife is mentioned, teaching that he ruled through her, for she was a daughter of great and wealthy men. Eight kings are counted here and eleven alufim, corresponding to which eleven judges were appointed over Israel from Joshua until Samuel, and eight kings until Joram. And this is ואלכה לנגדך."], :book :genesis, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 36, :notes {1 "The phrase ואלכה לנגדך (\"and I will go toward you\") appears to be a notarikon or acronym whose expansion is not given in the text; translated hyper-literally as it stands."}, :source-witnesses [["Kitzur Baal HaTurim" "http://sefaria.org"] ["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:17:50.296051426Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}